128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (The increasing use of laptops for work, study, and entertainment has created a demand for ergonomic and portable workstation solutions. Conventional laptop tables, often made from wood or metal, are typically heavy, expensive, and difficult to store and transport. This project focuses on the design and fabrication of a lightweight, foldable, and cost-effective laptop table using WPVC \(Wood Polymer Composite\) material. WPVC was selected as the primary material due to its inherent properties of being lightweight, water-resistant, termite-proof, and easy to machine. The table consists of a WPVC tabletop supported by foldable legs attached using metal hinges. The design process involved measuring, marking, and precisely cutting the WPVC board, followed by drilling, assembly, and finishing. The final product is easy to fold into a compact form, facilitating efficient storage and portability. Testing confirmed its stability under normal laptop loads and its robust construction. The total manufacturing cost was found to be significantly lower compared to commercially available alternatives. This project successfully demonstrates the viability of using WPVC to create an affordable, lightweight, and practical solution for modern portable computing needs.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
