/E (The modern lifestyle heavily relies on portable computing devices like laptops. Using them on a desk is standard, but for many, working from a bed, sofa, or floor is a common occurrence. This has led to the popularity of laptop tables. Traditional laptop tables are typically crafted from wood, engineered wood \(MDF/Plywood\), or metal. While functional, these materials contribute to a product that can be heavy, bulky, and inconvenient to move or store, especially in small living spaces.)
/Pg 14 0 R
